# Auto-ship (GitHub PR + GCP) — default for user-visible site work

When the user asks for site features, landing pages, or says **ship**, **push**, **PR**, or **make it live**:

## Ship command (only path)

```powershell
git add <scoped files only>
git commit -m "…"
npm run ship
```

Push to `cursor/*` → auto-open PR → auto-merge to `main-fixed` → auto-deploy Cloud Run (~10 min).

**Do not** use `gcloud builds submit` or `npm run deploy:gcp` for routine work.

## Commit hygiene

- One fresh `cursor/<name>-c7f3` branch per PR from `origin/main-fixed`
- Never reuse a branch after squash-merge
- Never stage: `greenteam/`, `.worktrees/`, `aibhive-main-fixed/`, `public/*.apk`, `**/*.epub`, release binaries
- APKs download from Firebase (`public/diagnose-mobile-releases.json`) — not git

